2 Usage
*******

Use ‘M-x typst-watch-mode’ to start or stop a buffer-local ‘typst watch’
process.

   The main commands are:

typst-watch-start
     Start ‘typst watch’ for the current file.

typst-watch-stop
     Stop the buffer-local watch process.

typst-watch-compile
     Run ‘typst compile’ and open the output PDF.

typst-watch-preview
     Open the current output PDF.

typst-watch-compile-and-preview
     Compile the current file and open the output PDF.

   typst-watch-mode binds ‘C-c ! w’ to toggle the watcher, ‘C-c ! c’ to
compile, and ‘C-c ! p’ to preview.

   When typst-watch-auto-mode is enabled, typst-ts-compile,
typst-ts-preview, and typst-ts-compile-and-preview open the PDF viewer
after they run, when those commands are available.


File: typst-watch.info,  Node: Configuration,  Next: Development,  Prev: Usage,  Up: Top

3 Configuration
***************

Set typst-watch-pdf-viewer to force a viewer:

     (setq typst-watch-pdf-viewer "zathura")

   When typst-watch-pdf-viewer is nil, typst-watch tries ‘zathura’ and
then ‘evince’.  Change the fallback with
typst-watch-fallback-pdf-viewer.

   Set typst-watch-typst-command when Typst is not on PATH.

   Set typst-watch-output-file-function to customise the output PDF
path.  The function receives the Typst source path and must return the
PDF path.


